EULER IDENTITY (COMPOUNDING LIMIT)
515.1 analysis

e^{i\pi} = -1

Special case of
e^{i\theta} = cos\theta + i sin\theta
at \theta = \pi

Limit that produces it
lim (n\to\infty) (1 + i\pi/n)^n = e^{i\pi}

TYPES AND VARIABLES
n     positive integer (steps \to \infty)
\theta real angle in radians (\theta=\pi)
i     imaginary unit, i^{2} = -1
z     complex number a + bi
1 + i\pi/n   one infinitesimal rotation factor

GEOMETRIC MECHANISM
Start at 1 + 0i
Each multiply by (1 + i\pi/n) rotates by \approx \pi/n
n steps accumulate exactly \pi radians (half-turn)
Polygonal chain \to unit semicircle from +1 to -1

FINITE-n SNAPSHOTS
n=2    overshoots, ~3.18 short of -1
n=3    still coarse, ~2.37 short
n=20   close, 0.28 short
n=60   0.086 short and tightening

In the limit the discrete path becomes the smooth arc and the identity appears.
